t\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>CamTech Cultural Day Khmer traditional games have been associated with the lives of the Cambodian people for a long time. In the past, our ancestors normally played these games in the autumn after the harvest season, especially during the traditional Khmer New Year celebration. The Khmer traditional games that were popularly played at that time were Bos Angkunh, Leak Kanseng, Sdach Jong, Teanh Prot, Krong Me Moan, etc. The aesthetic value of all these games is based on the ideals embedded in the games by Khmer ancestors to reflect the realities of life of the ancient Khmer people at that time, along with many folk legends that have been narrated from mouth to mouth. Can you guess what games will be played on Songkran Day at the Camtech University? Do not forget to join our activity and make your guess for a chance to win prizes from our team. To participate in this activity, each individual needs to follow three easy conditions as below: 1. Like the official Facebook page of Camtech University, 2. Mention at least 3 friends,3. Share this announcement publicly. The winners will be announced on April 7, 2022. Related Events<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":14628,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"elementor_header_footer","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[180],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-14627","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-event"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/14627","targetHints